      "id": "web-pdf",
      "prompt": "https://sleepnomad.github.io/hermes-trismegistus/ Can you extract all the content here into a well formatted and designed PDF?"
    },
    {
      "id": "arabic-pdf",
      "prompt": "نسخة PDF منسقة وجميلة من جميع محتويات notes.txt من فضلك. احتفظ بالنص الإنجليزي كما هو داخل الملف.",
      "files": {
        "notes.txt": "FIELD REPORT: TIDAL GARDENS\n\nOverview\nThe tidal garden pilot began on 14 March 2025. Its purpose is to measure how planted barriers reduce coastal erosion.\n\nSites\nSite Amber has 24 planting beds and a 120 metre shoreline. Site Cobalt has 18 beds and a 95 metre shoreline. Site Jade has 30 beds and a 150 metre shoreline.\n\nMeasurements\nAmber recorded a sediment gain of 12 millimetres. Cobalt recorded 8 millimetres. Jade recorded 17 millimetres. These preliminary observations are not proof of long term effectiveness.\n\nMethods\nEach site was measured at the same tidal stage. Three samples were collected from each planting bed. Measurements were repeated after six weeks.\n\nLimitations\nThe pilot did not include an unplanted control site. Seasonal variation and storm effects remain unresolved. The team should repeat sampling over a full year.\n\nNext steps\nInstall control transects, publish measurement protocols, and schedule quarterly surveys. The next review is on 30 September 2025.\n\nSource note\nThis is a synthetic benchmark fixture, not a scientific publication. END OF FIELD REPORT.\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "csv",
      "prompt": "A file named totals.csv with the totals by region from sales.json, please. Use the columns region,total and alphabetical region order.",
      "files": {
        "sales.json": "[{\"region\":\"West\",\"amount\":12.5},{\"region\":\"East\",\"amount\":20},{\"region\":\"West\",\"amount\":7.5},{\"region\":\"North\",\"amount\":3}]\n"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "read-only",
      "prompt": "Explain in two sentences what a PDF is. Do not use tools or create or change any files.",
      "readOnly": true,
      "files": {
        "untouched.txt": "This file must not change.\n"
      }
    }
  ],
